  "summary": "A common resident. A thickset, heavy-billed yellow canary. The male is dark green above and on the breast. The female is paler above and entirely yellow below. Southern birds are duller olive-green with dark-streaked upper parts. Northern birds are paler, more yellow and smaller. The immature is duller. The song is slower, huskier and less tuneful than other canaries. The Kemp name is Bully Canary and the code NB was left unchanged.",
